🕸️ Firecrawl REST API — Complete Reference Guide
 
Version: v2 (Current Stable) | Base URL:  https://api.firecrawl.dev/v2  | Protocol: REST + JSON | Auth: Bearer Token (API Key)
 
 
 
🎯 Overview
 
Firecrawl is a web intelligence & scraping API that turns websites into clean LLM-ready data (Markdown/JSON). Features:
 
- ✅ JavaScript rendering (headless browser)
- ✅ Single-page scrape / Bulk crawl / Site map
- ✅ Browser automation (click, wait, scroll, execute JS) 
- ✅ AI data extraction (structured JSON)
- ✅ Search + retrieval
- ✅ Webhooks / Async tasks
- ✅ Open-source + MCP/CLI/SDKs 
 
 
 
🔐 Authentication
 
Method: Bearer Token (API Key)
Header:  Authorization: Bearer YOUR_API_KEY 
Get Key: Dashboard → API Keys (https://firecrawl.com/dashboard) 
 
bash
  
# Standard request format
curl -X POST https://api.firecrawl.dev/v2/scrape \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer fc-..." \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"url":"https://example.com"}'
 
 
 
 
🌐 Base URLs & Versions
 
- v2 (Recommended):  https://api.firecrawl.dev/v2 
- v1 (Legacy):  https://api.firecrawl.dev/v1 
- OpenAPI Spec: https://docs.firecrawl.dev/api-reference/v2-openapi.json 
 
 
 
📋 Core Endpoints
 
📍 Scrape — Single Page
 
 POST /scrape  — Scrape one URL, return clean content
 
Request Body:
 
json
  
{
  "url": "https://example.com",
  "formats": ["markdown", "html", "rawHtml", "screenshot", "pdf"],
  "onlyMainContent": true,
  "includeTags": [],
  "excludeTags": ["nav", "footer"],
  "headers": {},
  "waitFor": 2000,
  "actions": [
    {"type": "click", "selector": "#load-more"},
    {"type": "wait", "milliseconds": 1000},
    {"type": "scroll", "direction": "down"}
  ],
  "location": {
    "country": "US",
    "languages": ["en-US"]
  },
  "mobile": false,
  "removeBase64Images": true
}
